<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fu Sheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">335–357</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fu Sheng was emperor of the Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> state in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 355 to 357. The son of Fu Jian, founder of the state, he is described in the histories as violent and cruel, executing officials and relatives at will. In 357 his cousin Fu Jian overthrew and killed him and took the title Heavenly King, beginning the reign that brought Former Qin to the height of its power.</p></div>
